---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const updated = "11 July 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Studio — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Studio, the native Mac performance capture and voice conversion app by DataIsland Software LLC, part of the PolySpeak suite."
>

  <section class="legal fade-in">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/privacy">← All Privacy Policies</a></div>

    <h1>Studio — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">DataIsland Software LLC &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      Studio is a native Mac performance-capture and voice-conversion app, part of the
      PolySpeak voice-production suite. This policy explains exactly what data Studio
      accesses — including its use of the microphone — and confirms that nothing it
      processes ever leaves your device.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Studio makes no network requests of any kind.</strong> Recording, importing,
      and voice conversion all run entirely on your Mac using a local voice pipeline.
      Studio does use your microphone to capture performance takes, but only while you are
      actively recording, and only with your explicit permission. The app has no server,
      no account, and no analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What Studio Accesses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Microphone</strong> — used for live in-app recording of performance takes.
        This requires the standard macOS microphone permission prompt, and the microphone
        is only active while you are actively recording
      </li>
      <li>Audio files you explicitly import</li>
      <li>The shared local voice-library folder, read to populate the voice-conversion picker</li>
      <li><code>.studiosession</code> files you open or create</li>
      <li>A nearby <code>.polyproject</code> manifest file, if one exists, which Studio may write export records into</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Studio does not access your camera, contacts, location, photos, or calendar.
    </p>

    <h2>What Leaves Your Device</h2>

    <h3>Nothing</h3>
    <p>
      As with TableRead, Studio's voice conversion runs a local Python/RVC pipeline via
      subprocess entirely on your Mac. No recorded audio, no imported audio, and no
      converted audio is ever uploaded anywhere. Microphone input captured during
      recording is written to a local audio file and processed on-device — it is never
      transmitted over the network, to DataIsland, or to any third party.
    </p>

    <h2>What Is Stored Locally</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Session files</strong> (<code>.studiosession</code>) — takes list, character assignments, and selected voice, saved to locations you choose</li>
      <li><strong>Imported, recorded, converted, and exported audio files</strong> — saved to locations you choose on your Mac</li>
      <li><strong>The shared voice library</strong> — local voice models used for conversion</li>
    </ul>
    <p>None of this data is synced to iCloud or transmitted to DataIsland.</p>

    <h2>What Studio Does Not Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Does not transmit microphone audio, or any other data, anywhere</li>
      <li>Does not require an account or login</li>
      <li>Does not collect analytics, usage statistics, or crash reports</li>
      <li>Does not access your microphone except while you are actively recording</li>
      <li>Does not access your files without your explicit action</li>
      <li>Does not share data with third parties</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Studio is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
      information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the "Last updated" date above.
      Continued use of Studio after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:<br />
      <a href="mailto:support@dataisland.com">support@dataisland.com</a><br />
      DataIsland Software LLC
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .legal h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .meta { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .legal h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .legal p  { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }

  ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gray-dark);
  }

  ul li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
